{"name":"Painted Turtle","hex":"#56745f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"painted turtle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common American freshwater turtle (Chrysemys picta), with red, orange and yellow markings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painted_turtle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Painted turtle","blocks":[{"text":"The painted turtle is North America's most widespread native turtle, with a rich evolutionary history that stretches back 15 million years. As resilient survivors belonging to the pond turtle family Emydidae, these turtles adapted creatively to the planet's changing climate. During the last Ice Age, they split into distinct groups and evolved into three regionally unique subspecies: the Eastern painted turtle, the Midland painted turtle, and the Western painted turtle. Scientists still debate whether a fourth group, the Southern painted turtle, is its own separate species or another subspecies. Because they are highly adaptable and widely distributed across fresh waters from Canada to Mexico, their conservation status is listed as Least Concern, meaning they are currently thriving in the wild."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Painted_turtle_%28Chrysemys_picta%29_Madden_Haag.jpg/330px-Painted_turtle_%28Chrysemys_picta%29_Madden_Haag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painted_turtle","wikidata":"Q199203"},{"title":"Paint","blocks":[{"text":"Paint is a material or mixture of colored liquid that, when applied to a solid material and allowed to dry, adds a film-like layer. As art, this is used to create an image or images known as a painting. Paint can be made in many colors and types. Most paints are either oil-based or water-based, and each has distinct characteristics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Multicolored_tempera_paints.jpg/330px-Multicolored_tempera_paints.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint","wikidata":"Q174219"},{"title":"Turtle","blocks":[{"text":"Turtles are reptiles characterized by a special shell developed mainly from their ribs. Modern turtles are divided into two major groups, the Pleurodira and Cryptodira, which differ in the way the head retracts. There are 360 living and recently extinct species of turtles, including land-dwelling tortoises and freshwater terrapins. They are found on most continents, some islands and, in the case of sea turtles, much of the ocean. Like other amniotes they breathe air and do not lay eggs underwater, although many species live in or around water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Turtle_diversity.jpg/330px-Turtle_diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle","wikidata":"Q223044"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Schneider_Johann_Gottlob_1750-1822.png/330px-Schneider_Johann_Gottlob_1750-1822.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Schneider_Johann_Gottlob_1750-1822.png/330px-Schneider_Johann_Gottlob_1750-1822.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"German naturalist Johann Gottlob Schneider first categorized the painted turtle.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchneider_Johann_Gottlob_1750-1822.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Painted-Turtle-1_Young.jpg/330px-Painted-Turtle-1_Young.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Painted-Turtle-1_Young.jpg/330px-Painted-Turtle-1_Young.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm